# Monitor: BeeGFS client (`beegfs_client`)

## Detection

- Enumerate mounts with fstype **`beegfs`** or **`beegfs_nodev`** (`/proc/mounts`).
- Device id is the **mount path** (e.g. `/scratch`).
- `/proc/fs/beegfs/<clientID>/` on BeeGFS **7.3.x** exposes config/state only — **no** cumulative I/O counter files (`ops-rd` / `MiB-rd` absent). Do not invent procfs counter parsers for 7.3.x.

## Capacity (cheap, every sample)

- `statvfs(3)` on the mount → `fs_bytes_*` / `fs_files_*` (same semantics as `lustre_llite`).

## I/O and metadata (bounded `beegfs-ctl`)

- On 7.3.x there is **no public linkable clientstats library**; use **`beegfs-ctl --clientstats`** (`--nodetype=storage` and `--nodetype=meta`).
- Prefer **`--rwunit=B`** when supported (`B-rd` / `B-wr`); else parse `MiB-rd` / `MiB-wr` (scientific notation OK) and scale **× 1048576** to `vfs_read_bytes` / `vfs_write_bytes`.
- Map ctl abbreviations to portable **`vfs_*`** keys (see `beegfs_client.h`); never emit raw `MiB-rd` / `ops-rd` / `unlnk` as KEY names.
- **Never** ingest the cluster **`Sum:`** line as this host’s counters — select the **local** line via hostname / short hostname / local IPv4.
- Pass **`--mount=<mnt>`** when supported; keep wall-time budget on ctl (timeout → skip; first-fail log; capacity still works).
- **Jitter:** when `enable_slow_tier` is on, refresh ctl only on **`COLLECT_FULL`**; when off, at most once per `max(sample_freq, 30s)`. Emit ctl-derived keys only on refresh ticks (tier table marks `vfs_*` slow; `fs_*` stay fast).

## Configure

- **`--enable-beegfs`** default **yes**; `MONITOR_WITH_BEEGFS`; capability slug fragment **`beegfs`**.
- Missing `beegfs-ctl` with mounts present: detect + capacity still work; **no** per-sample ERROR spam.

## Tests

- Schema contract rejects raw ctl names; ctl parse fixtures cover Sum ignore, MiB→bytes, hostname match.

